  <name>Nuage</name>
  <summary>Your cloud storage as a regular folder</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.felixilgatto">
    <name>Nuage contributors</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Nuage shows your cloud storage accounts as folders of your home, like
      any other folder: files open in your usual applications and are
      downloaded only when you use them. Changes are uploaded in the
      background.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Set up an account in a few screens, signed in through your browser</li>
      <li>See what is syncing, pause and resume uploads</li>
      <li>Browse, upload, move and share files, even when an account is not mounted</li>
      <li>Keep folders or patterns out of the sync</li>
      <li>Google Docs open in your web browser</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Nuage uses rclone. Google Drive, OneDrive, Dropbox, pCloud, Nextcloud,
      WebDAV and S3 bucket storage are supported; for Google Drive, your own
      sign-in client keeps your access private to you.
    </p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.felixilgatto.Nuage.desktop</launchable>
